Z||000000||martin1875||11-11-2000||02:30 AM||||i am looking for some information on rebuild kits for my fiero. i have an 86 2.8 v6. i want to know if any one has brought a performance overhaul kit from the fiero store.i just want a litte extra power.does anyone know how much horsepower you can getout of the 2.8 without an turbo or nitrous.can any one tell me if the performance camshaft is worth the time and money. thank you for any help you can offer||||reg||1
Z||000001||maninblack||11-11-2000||03:49 AM||||i think hte kit from the fierostore would roughly gives you 20-30 hp.but while you are doing it ,I think you might also want to <BR>polish your heads and intake or even install<BR>a larger t-body for another 15-20 hp||||reg||1
Z||000002||martin1875||11-11-2000||12:22 PM||||thanks for the information. do you think the kits price of $900.00 is worth it. or would i be just as happy with the stock kit and a different cam.where could i get a larger TB<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||88formula||11-11-2000||03:29 PM||||The Fiero Store prices are way too high for those kits. Buy the components from a place like Northern Auto Parts.  But with that kit you can expect about 160 horsepower according to Dyno2000. 175-180 horsepower is the max I would expect from a fiero 2.8-liter engine done with traditional modifications without going nuts on the money, naturally aspired.<P> <A HREF="http://www.northernautoparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.northernautoparts.com/</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_Freak||11-11-2000||08:09 PM||||Yeah... definately go with someone else.  I'm purchasing my kit from Summit.  You can interchange any of the parts you wish.  I wouldn't expect that much from the bumped up pistons, especially for the price.  Go with the Cam and Springs....and save the money for a turbo.<BR>||||reg||1
